        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.152,
            0.485,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "1. Find the missing terms:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.246,
            0.178,
            0.866,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "a. Perimeter of a rectangle = 14 cm; breadth = 2 cm; length = ?."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.246,
            0.204,
            0.785,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "b. Perimeter of a square = 20 cm; side of a length = ?."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.23,
            0.859,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "c. Perimeter of a rectangle = 12 m; length = 3 m; breadth = ?."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.259,
            0.885,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "2. A rectangle having sidelengths 5 cm and 3 cm is made using a piece of wire. If the wire is straightened and then bent to form a square, what will be the length of a side of the square?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.328,
            0.885,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "3. Find the length of the third side of a triangle having a perimeter of 55 cm and having two sides of length 20 cm and 14 cm, respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.397,
            0.884,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "4. What would be the cost of fencing a rectangular park whose length is 150 m and breadth is 120 m, if the fence costs \\`40 per metre?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.446,
            0.884,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "5. A piece of string is 36 cm long. What will be the length of each side, if it is used to form:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.494,
            0.389,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "a. A square,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.518,
            0.728,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": "b. A triangle with all sides of equal length, and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.545,
            0.884,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "c. A hexagon (a six sided closed figure) with sides of equal length?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.595,
            0.885,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "6. A farmer has a rectangular field having length 230 m and breadth 160 m. He wants to fence it with 3 rounds of rope as shown. What is the total length of rope needed?"
        },
